## Coverage and conclusions

| Criterion / scenario | Located cross-reference evidence | Observed conclusion |
| --- | --- | --- |
| SC-001: atomic task closure | Completion: Task commit contract; Git: Work and prepare the boundary | Both require verified result, current evidence and initial owning checkbox in the closing commit; a final checklist or merge summary cannot substitute. |
| SC-002: subject and ownership | Completion: Task commit contract; Git: persistence audit paragraph | Exactly one leading owning ID and one executable closure; non-task campaign and merge commits do not invent task IDs. |
| SC-003: partial and parent status | Completion: partial-checkpoint paragraph, Parent completion and stopping; Git: audit paragraph | Authorized partial work stays unchecked; the later closing boundary references it. Parent-only follow-ups cannot excuse detached initial task closure. |
| SC-004: publication cadence | Completion: Complete and commit each task step 6; Git: Publish each commit | Task and ancillary report/status/merge commits publish before any further work/commit. Direct focused calls follow the same cadence; explicit scoped user exceptions remain exceptions. |
| SC-005: failed/uncertain publication | Completion: step 6; Git: Publish each commit, Platform authorization rejection | Preserve the commit and stop advancement. Inspection, readback and scoped recovery remain possible; no alternate workflow accumulates unpublished work. |
| SC-006: interrupted audit/recovery | Completion: Task persistence audit and recovery; Git: Continue a blocked workflow | Audit actual closing diffs and relevant merge parents within the active range. Invalid published history remains invalid after a forward correction; no silent rewrite or task replay. |
| SC-007: integration scope | Completion: Integrate the completed boundary; Git: Work and prepare the boundary | A main subset in an incomplete phase pushes and pauses. A coherent authorized revision boundary uses its own eligibility gate. |
| SC-008: interrupted merge | Completion: final integration paragraph; Git: Merge, verify, and publish, Continue a blocked workflow | Explicit two-parent merge, merged checks and target push establish integrated completion. A verified merge awaiting publication needs its existing push, not a duplicate merge. |

Eight actual source-presence assertions passed under Python with bytecode disabled; manual semantic cross-reading supports the conclusions above. These assertions are corroboration of located clauses, not behavioral task/merge fixtures. No confirmed inconsistency was found in this focused scope; canonical defect/recommendation/evidence-gap finding count is zero. No source correction queue is proposed.

## Evidence and limits

Actual orientation checked current HEAD/branch, clean worktree, empty staged diff, no unmerged entries, worktree occupancy, local refs and exact LOCAL remote parent ref. Identity allocation inspected only path/ref names across reviews, features and phase-nested revisions: highest reserved sequence 041, so this child uses 042. Frozen packages including 038–041 were not loaded or edited. Parent evidence was consulted only for current unfinished scope and suspension ownership.

Scoped final artifact checks cover Markdown heading separation and local links in this child report and new child navigation, exact protected tracked file hashes and the owned diff. Existing historical navigation links are excluded from current validation. Governing source hashes must remain identical. The support suite is not run: no implementation, acceptance tooling or plugin package source changes occur. Live client activation, actual task execution, interruption transport loss, push denial and conflicted-merge recovery are not executed here. No broad prerelease or product-readiness claim follows.

The external authorized observation record retains exact loaded-resource hashes, separate command stdout/stderr/exit codes from durable capture onward, original visible tool chunk identities and early truncation limits. It will retain report/publication/integration identities and actual delegated acceptance separately from this committed assessment. No transaction journal is introduced into the project.

## Acceptance and stopping

Present this concrete report, child README, shared navigation delta and parent suspension entry to the delegated coordinator after commit publication/readback, with their exact blobs/hashes and scoped checks. Do not conclude or integrate the child before acceptance. Upon accepted bounded record integration, refresh the parent target, explicitly merge the complete verified child tip, check the merged result, commit and immediately publish/read back the parent target. Git integration summary and external observations retain actual integration/publication identities without a post-closure report edit. Return on the parent branch and stop with parent execution suspended.
